          %h2#black_hole_entropy Black hole entropy
          %p
            In (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"}> perturbative
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            associated to a macroscopic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            finds an explanation as follows:
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            is regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+QFT"} strongly coupled
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensate"} condensate
            of string states (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+strings"}> closed strings
            , carrying
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+space"} Minkowski space
            that is known to turn into the black hole spacetime as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling"} string coupling
            is turned on. Such turn out to be certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            configurations in Minkowski space: at weak coupling the D-brane does not back-react on the spacetime (since that back-reaction is mediated by closed string quanta) and so it just sits there, whereas at strong coupling it curves spacetime and may collapse to a configuration that looks like the prescribed black hole spacetime.
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BlackBrane.png"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#IbanezUranga12"} Ibanez-Uranga 12
          %p
            Now, if the configuration has a sufficient amount of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            preserved (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"}> BPS state
            ), then one argues (
            %a{:href => "#Witten95"}> Witten 95, section 2.3
            ) that certain observables are actually independent of the coupling constant (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/protection+from+quantum+corrections"}> protection from quantum corrections
            ”), and accordingly these observables are the same for black holes as for the corresponding D-brane configurations in flat space, where they may be computed in string perturbation theory.
          %p
            The best studied such configuration is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D1-D5+brane+bound+states"} D1-D5 brane bound states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            (which are “protected”), hence the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            (
            %a{:href => "#StromingerVafa96"}> Strominger-Vafa 96
            ), see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Witten+genus#RelationToBPSStateCounting"} Witten genus – Relation to BPS state counting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            of the corresponding (supersymmetric) black hole. And indeed the results match the semiclassical BH-entropy to leading order and in addition provide their higher order quantum corrections. See the
            %em
              %a{:href => "#References"} References
            below.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dual
            version of the D1/D5-bound states are D0/D6-bound states, coming from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Nelson93"} Nelson 93
